OL,3,GNEWSAGraves of missing WW1 soldiers
OL,4,Afound
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe graves of two lost World War One
OL,7,Fsoldiers from the north-west of England
OL,8,Fhave been found in Belgium and France
OL,9,Fmore than a century after their deaths.
OL,11,FLieutenant Fred Naylor from Aspull, in
OL,12,FWigan, and Company Sergeant Major
OL,13,FHerbert Bannister, of Wavertree,
OL,14,FLiverpool, died in March and April 1918
OL,15,Fand were both named on memorials to the
OL,16,Fmissing.
OL,18,FNaylor was first identified as "unknown
OL,19,Fsoldier" by badges on his uniform, the
OL,20,FCommonwealth War Graves Commission
OL,21,F(CWGC) said.
OL,23,APub: 19-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
